a delimiter inside a quoted field:
  0: [name] | [city]
  1: [Ada] | [London, UK]
a doubled quote is one quote:
  0: [quote]
  1: [she said "hi"]
a quoted field may span lines:
  0: [id] | [note]
  1: [1] | [line one\nline two]

empty fields are preserved:
  0: [a] | [] | [c]
CRLF is accepted on input:
  0: [a] | [b]
  1: [1] | [2]
a missing final newline is fine:
  0: [a] | [b]
blank lines are skipped:
  0: [a] | [b]
  1: [c] | [d]

tab-separated:
  0: [a] | [b]
  1: [1] | [2]
semicolon-separated:
  0: [a] | [b]
  1: [1] | [2]
with comment lines:
  0: [a] | [b]
  1: [1] | [2]
trimming unquoted padding:
  0: [a] | [b]

sniffed delimiter byte = 59   (';' is 59)
parsed with it:
  0: [name] | [address] | [zip]
  1: [Ada] | [1, High St] | [E1]

line 1: 2 fields, first=id
line 2: 2 fields, first=1
line 3: 2 fields, first=2
line 5: 2 fields, first=3
error = unterminated quoted field at line 1
what survived:
  0: [a] | [never closed\n]

quoting is applied only where needed:
  plain   -> abc
  comma   -> "a,b"
  quote   -> "say ""hi"""
  newline -> "a\nb"

csv_write:
name,city
Ada,"London, UK"
Grace,"say ""hi"""

round trip:
  0: [name] | [city]
  1: [Ada] | [London, UK]
  2: [Grace] | [say "hi"]
built by hand:
x,42,"a,b"
y,7,plain

wrote file = true
read back:
  0: [id] | [note]
  1: [1] | [has, comma]
  2: [2] | [has\nnewline]
streamed 3 records, 6 fields
missing file = 0 rows
